/-!
# Native Čech-class transport to finite closed fibres

The literal pulled-back cover and cocycle give an actual map of the
original Čech extensions. Its endpoints are the given coefficient map
and the canonical map of native integer sheaves into pushforward.
Consequently the genuine finite-pushforward cohomology equivalence
sends the mapped original class to the class of the restricted cocycle.

No higher-direct-image base-change isomorphism or local-freeness theorem
is asserted here.
-/
